  "note": "Municipal elections, May 1952. Fifteen councillorships (five in each ward) were filled without a contest; the six aldermen had been elected three years earlier and were not due for re-election (Fermanagh Herald, 24 May 1952, p. 6). Unionist nominees, returned unopposed. Jackson and McCutcheon replaced Cecil Whaley and Jack Mercer. Returned unopposed."
